# .dockerignore: what never goes into the Docker build context (see Dockerfile).
# BUSINESS: no secrets and no locally generated data in an image that goes on the
#   internet. The tape is generated inside the image from the seed.
# TECH: `docker build .` sends the repo folder to the builder; these patterns are left
#   out. That keeps the build fast and stops local, Windows-built files (venv,
#   node_modules, dist) from overwriting the clean Linux ones the Dockerfile makes.
#   "**/" matches the name in any folder, not just the repo root.

# Git history and local tool settings
.git
.claude

# Secrets: never in an image
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Python virtual environments and caches
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/.pytest_cache
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov

# Node packages and build output (rebuilt inside the image)
**/node_modules
frontend/dist

# Generated tape (rebuilt inside the image from the seed)
data/

# End-to-end test output
e2e/test-results
e2e/playwright-report
